## Bold & Moody Fall Nail Ideas (Plum, Forest Green, Black)

Most people avoid the darkest end of the fall palette because they assume it reads as trying too hard. The opposite is true this season. A deep plum or forest green, worn as a single confident colour with no nail art at all, is one of the most effortless looks on this entire list, and it takes less time to apply than half the trends above it.

Plum sits as purple's more grown-up, more wearable cousin, muted enough to pair with nearly every fall outfit without matching anything specifically. Matte finish is doing the heavy lifting here for 2026: a glossy plum reads pretty, but a matte plum reads intentional and editorial, the difference between a colour you picked and a colour you meant. Forest green and olive earn a similar treatment. Deep, earthy green has moved from an occasional accent into a full-set colour this year, and it flatters a wider range of skin than people expect, particularly with warm undertones.

Black gets a place here too, though the most current version rarely commits to flat black across the whole hand. A plum-black or "vampy" gel, dark enough to photograph nearly black but with actual colour underneath in direct light, gives you the drama without the starkness. For anyone chasing a full moody manicure without going that dark, teal is worth a mention as the season's unexpected wildcard, a blue-green that still reads distinctly autumnal despite not appearing on anyone's traditional fall palette a few years ago.

